# Medusa Fork — Core Rules

`packages/medusa-fork/` is the canonical Medusa v2.14.1 source. MercFlow owns this codebase.

## Where to make changes

- **Medusa behaviour or entity changes** → edit in `packages/medusa-fork/`
- **MercFlow module behaviour** → edit in `packages/*/src/`
- **`node_modules/`** → never touch, ever

## Dependency rules (post-M0)

After fork-setup (M0) is complete, `@medusajs/*` runtime dependencies must always be `workspace:*` — never an npm version string.

```json
// ✅ After M0
"@medusajs/framework": "workspace:*"

// ❌ Never after M0
"@medusajs/framework": "2.14.1"
```

## Every new entity in the fork needs `store_id`

Any new DML model or MikroORM entity added to `packages/medusa-fork/` that represents tenant-scoped data **must** include `store_id` from day one:

```ts
// ✅
const MyEntity = model.define("my_entity", {
  id: model.id(),
  store_id: model.text(),   // required — tenant discriminator
  // ...
})

// ❌ Missing store_id on tenant-scoped entity
const MyEntity = model.define("my_entity", {
  id: model.id(),
  name: model.text(),
})
```

## Upstream cherry-picks

Never apply Medusa upstream commits to `packages/medusa-fork/` without explicit written instruction from the user. Each cherry-pick is a deliberate decision, not routine maintenance.

## Subpath exports

`packages/medusa-fork/medusa/package.json` exports must preserve all subpaths used across the codebase:

- `@medusajs/medusa/fulfillment`
- `@medusajs/medusa/fulfillment-manual`
- `@medusajs/framework/mikro-orm/core`
- `@medusajs/framework/mikro-orm/migrations`
- `@medusajs/framework/http`
- `@medusajs/framework/utils`
- `@medusajs/framework/types`

Verify with `pnpm typecheck` before committing any `package.json` change in the fork.
